    "measurement_limits": [
      "Regex is a new API; supplemental workloads have no pre-feature counterpart.",
      "Regex compile measures PCRE2 compilation; repeated search reuses the compiled program and includes operation-local coordinate mapping, native work buffers and normal GC.",
      "Capture and limit workloads initialize global patterns before timing and establish the retained-memory baseline after warm-up; persistent_bytes includes the live program and globals.",
      "hasMatch checks both GC object count and accounted bytes against the pre-search baseline. Temporary work buffers are released on each operation; all reported retained_bytes counters are zero.",
      "PCRE2 interpreter budgets: match 1000000, depth 1000, heap 8192 KiB; UTF/UCP enabled, JIT disabled, Unicode 17.0.0.",
      "Backtracking has no general linear-time guarantee. Configured counters are not wall-clock timeouts.",
      "Variation and ratios are observations from one Windows x64 machine; small differences are not causal speedup claims.",
      "Primary VM comparison uses 0.5-second calibrated samples and nine randomly interleaved repetitions per case; regex supplemental samples use 0.2 seconds and five repetitions."
    ]
